  <section class="mp-section mp-paper" id="handoff"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">02 / What reaches your sales team</p><h2>A meeting your seller<br>can prepare for.</h2><p class="mp-section-lead">The useful deliverable is the conversation and the information needed to develop it.</p><ul class="mp-checks"><li>Why the account belongs in the campaign.</li><li>Who accepted and what they are responsible for.</li><li>The buyer’s reason for taking the meeting.</li><li>What they agreed to discuss.</li><li>Questions still open and who owns the next step.</li></ul><p>Track a booking, an attended meeting, a sales-accepted conversation and an opportunity separately. <a href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">Use the Meeting Quality Check</a> to follow those stages.</p></div><aside class="mp-note" aria-labelledby="mp-handoff-heading"><p class="mp-label">Illustrative handoff / ERP provider</p><h3 id="mp-handoff-heading">A workflow worth exploring.</h3><dl><div><dt>Account</dt><dd>Manufacturer with several production sites.</dd></div><div><dt>Contact</dt><dd>Operations director responsible for order changes.</dd></div><div><dt>Confirmed issue</dt><dd>Changes move between the ERP and shop floor through manual updates.</dd></div><div><dt>Meeting purpose</dt><dd>Understand the workflow and assess where integration could help.</dd></div><div><dt>Open questions</dt><dd>IT involvement, project priority and budget ownership.</dd></div></dl><p class="mp-small">Illustration of the information structure. It is not a client record or campaign result.</p></aside></div></section>
  <section class="mp-section" id="fit"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">03 / Decide whether the work fits</p><h2>Ready to give outbound<br>a defined job?</h2></div><div class="mp-fit-grid"><div><h3>A useful starting position</h3><ul class="mp-checks"><li>An established B2B offer with a credible business benefit.</li><li>An audience that can be identified and reached.</li><li>Customer value and margin that support the investment.</li><li>Sellers with time to assess and progress meetings.</li></ul></div><div class="mp-fit-note"><h3>Bring the decisions only you can make.</h3><p>Your team approves product claims, market priorities and relevant proof; provides agreed CRM and calendar access; and owns demonstrations, proposals and commercial decisions.</p><p>If readiness is unclear, work through the six checks before scoping the engagement.</p><a class="mp-button" href="/b2b-lead-generation-audit/">Check Your Campaign Readiness <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="mp-route-note"><p><strong>A different gap?</strong> Recover an existing database through <a href="/services/lead-reactivation/">lead reactivation</a>, add a wider <a href="/services/outsourced-sdr/">outsourced SDR function</a>, or help your own callers through <a href="/services/sdr-training/">SDR training</a>.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="mp-section mp-proof" id="proof"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">04 / Published campaign evidence</p><h2>See the market,<br>the work and the result.</h2><p>Three B2B offers. Specific campaign periods. Read the context behind each outcome.</p></div>{% set proofCases = commercialServices.cases %}{% include "commercial/proof.njk" %}<div class="mp-experience"><div><strong>500,000+</strong><span>outbound calls</span></div><div><strong>1,000+</strong><span>sellers coached</span></div><div><strong>150+</strong><span>companies supported</span></div><div><strong>Fortune 100/500</strong><span>sales experience</span></div></div><p class="mp-proof-note">Combined professional experience behind CallTeam. <a href="/about/">Meet the team and understand our approach →</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="mp-section" id="investment"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">05 / Scope the investment</p><h2>Start with the work.<br>Make the economics clear.</h2><p class="mp-price">From US$4,000<span> / month</span></p><p>The campaign-ready starting program assumes usable target accounts or contacts, a defined offer and market, CRM and calendar access, and sellers ready for meetings.</p><p>New prospect research, licensed data, additional markets and extra resources affect the final scope. Most programs begin with an initial three-month engagement.</p><a class="mp-text-link" href="/pricing/">Read pricing and all starting assumptions →</a></div><aside class="mp-tool"><p class="mp-label">Use your own customer economics</p><h3>What would the campaign need to return?</h3><p>Model cost, customer value, margin and conversion assumptions. Change the inputs to reflect the proposal you are considering.</p><a class="mp-button" href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/">Calculate Your Campaign ROI <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="mp-small">An estimate built from your assumptions. Review the model before using it to make a purchase.</p></aside></div></section>
